The regex pattern `^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$` works as follows:
- `^[a-z0-9]+` - Starts with one or more lowercase letters or digits
- `(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*` - Optionally followed by groups of a hyphen and one or more lowercase letters/digits
- `$` - End of string

This ensures:
- No leading hyphens (must start with letter/digit)
- No trailing hyphens (must end with letter/digit)
- No consecutive hyphens (each hyphen must be followed by letter/digit)
- Only lowercase letters and digits allowed

